Kokoro-82M v1.0: an English text to speech model by hexgrad,
https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, released under the
Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The files in this folder are the ONNX export published by onnx-community,
https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX (Apache-2.0),
copied unchanged: the 8-bit model (onnx/model_quantized.onnx), the voices
af_heart and am_michael (voices/*.bin) and the tokenizer. Both model cards
are copied here (README.md, and kokoro-82m-card/README.md for hexgrad's).

Training data, as hexgrad's card states: audio in the public domain,
audio under permissive licences (Apache, MIT and similar), synthetic audio
made with permission, and this CC BY audio, credited as the licences ask:
- Koniwa `tnc` (https://github.com/koniwa/koniwa), under 1 hour,
  CC BY 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
- SIWIS French speech synthesis database
  (https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/2353), under 11 hours,
  CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
The base model is StyleTTS 2 (yl4579/StyleTTS2-LJSpeech, MIT).

No non-commercial condition applies: the model and what it speaks may be
used for any purpose. orOS names Kokoro and hexgrad where the voice is
downloaded. orOS downloads this folder on the person's device only when
they ask for the natural English voice.
